I also had problems configuring PuTTY properly with color. The key is
to make sure that you are using the latest version (.60). I was using
an older .58 distro and everything was coming up inverted rather than
in proper color.

Once you have the correct version, go into your configs under
Connection | Data and change the Terminal Type string to "xterm-
color".

If you want to use IBMGraphics, may also need to go under Window |
Translation and change the character set to "CP437"

There is also a thread on this topic in the help section of the
devnull bragging board with more info, including some putty reg files
for the various servers.    Once you get configured, be sure to join
Clan DYWYPI!

